{
  "why": "The host side of the gumball tool protocol (`📋️design.md` §5, `📓️w3-t-spatial-report.md` §2/§S2.5), stepped by the pure `worldGumballStep` of `🌐️World3dHost`: each step is one event and the ONE verb dispatch it owes (`null` = none). Local gestures dispatch one net delta on release with no `phase`; live gestures (`gumballLiveDispatch`) stream `phase: \"stream\"` ticks one in flight with the newest pose winning, commit the tail with `phase: \"commit\"`, and abort with the verb's identity delta, `phase: \"abort\"` and the `reason`. A case's `live`, `transformMode` and `targets` fill its `start` events and its `targets` its `release` events. Every guest that consumes these dispatches (fem 3d, lowpoly, generation 3d, …) replays them with the target ids replaced by one movable node of its own document and must publish exactly `guest.edits` edits moving it by `guest.offset`. Schema: `🧬️schema/🛠️gumball-live-protocol/🔣️.json`.",
